19:T587,## Modelling the essential

**Abstraction** is the art of modelling the **essential** and ignoring the **irrelevant**. It answers *what*, never *how*. When you describe a car as something that can `start()`, `accelerate()`, and `brake()`, you have abstracted away pistons, fuel injection, and a thousand wires — none of which the driver needs.

An **interface** (or an abstract type) IS an abstraction made concrete. A driver presses `brake()` and the car stops; the hydraulics, calipers, and ABS controller are simply not part of the picture they were handed.

## Why it matters

- It **reduces cognitive load**, you reason about three verbs, not three thousand components.
- It **decouples callers from internals**, code that holds a `Car` reference never names a piston, so the internals can change freely.

```
Car c = pickCar();
c.brake();   // the caller knows WHAT, never HOW
```

## Abstraction vs. encapsulation

These two are constantly confused. The distinction is clean:

- **Abstraction** is the **design view**, it hides *complexity* by exposing a simple surface (the *what*).
- **Encapsulation** is the **mechanism**, it hides *data* behind `private` walls and access methods (the *how it's protected*).

Abstraction decides which simple face to show; encapsulation is the lock that keeps the messy internals from leaking out. **Abstraction fights complexity; encapsulation enforces the boundary.**c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-foundations","activeLesson":"abstraction"}],["$","$L18","abstraction",{"lesson":{"id":"abstraction","patternId":"lld-foundations","title":"Abstraction","kind":"concept","difficulty":"Intro","statement":"Expose WHAT something does through a simple interface, and hide HOW it does it. Abstraction fights complexity; encapsulation enforces it.","companies":["Google","Amazon","Uber"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"The simple face","code":["interface Car {","    start(); accelerate(); brake();","}","","class PetrolCar implements Car {","    private pistons, valves, ecu;","    brake() { ignite(); injectFuel(); ... }","}"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":1,"narration":"Here is the abstraction: the Car interface. Three simple verbs, start, accelerate, brake. That is the entire surface anyone needs to know.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"driver","name":"Driver","methods":["+ commute()"],"x":0,"y":1},{"id":"car","name":"Car","stereotype":"interface","methods":["+ start()","+ accelerate()","+ brake()"],"x":1.4,"y":0.15,"tint":"accent"},{"id":"engine","name":"PetrolCar","fields":["- pistons","- valves","- ecu"],"methods":["+ start()","+ accelerate()","+ brake()","- ignite()","- injectFuel()"],"x":1.4,"y":1}],"relations":[{"id":"uses","from":"driver","to":"car","kind":"depend","label":"uses"},{"id":"impl","from":"engine","to":"car","kind":"implement"}],"shownClassIds":["car"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["car"]},"vars":[["abstraction","what, not how"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":2,"narration":"The Driver depends on the interface, nothing more. It only knows start/accelerate/brake, the contract, and never the machinery behind it.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["car","driver"],"shownRelIds":["uses"],"activeIds":["driver"]},"vars":[["⇢ uses","the contract only"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":5,"narration":"PetrolCar implements the interface, and look at its PRIVATE internals: pistons, valves, ecu, ignite(), injectFuel(). All the messy \"how\" lives here, hidden.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["car","driver","engine"],"shownRelIds":["uses","impl"],"activeIds":["engine"]},"vars":[["hidden","pistons / ignite / injectFuel"]]},{"view":"class","narration":"The Driver is shielded from every internal detail. Swap PetrolCar for ElectricCar, different internals entirely, and the Driver code does not change one line. That is abstraction.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["car","driver","engine"],"shownRelIds":["uses","impl"],"activeIds":[]},"vars":[["swap impl","caller unchanged ✓"]]}]},{"label":"One call, hidden steps","code":["driver.brake():","    car.brake()","        engage ABS","        apply calipers","        pump hydraulics","    return stopped"],"steps":[{"view":"sequence","codeLine":1,"narration":"Two lifelines: the Driver and the Car. Time flows downward. Watch how much happens behind a single simple call.","sequence":{"actors":[{"id":"d","label":"Driver","kind":"actor"},{"id":"c","label":"Car"}],"messages":[{"id":"m1","from":"d","to":"c","label":"brake()","kind":"call"},{"id":"m2","from":"c","to":"c","label":"engage ABS","kind":"self"},{"id":"m3","from":"c","to":"c","label":"apply calipers","kind":"self"},{"id":"m4","from":"c","to":"c","label":"pump hydraulics","kind":"self"},{"id":"m5","from":"c","to":"d","label":"stopped","kind":"return"}],"shownCount":0,"activeIndex":-1},"vars":[["lifelines","Driver, Car"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":2,"narration":"The Driver makes ONE simple call: brake(). That is the whole of the \"what\", a single verb, no parameters about hydraulics.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":1,"activeIndex":0},"vars":[["→ call","brake()"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":5,"narration":"Behind that one call, the Car runs a cascade of internal steps, engage ABS, apply calipers, pump hydraulics, that the Driver never sees.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":4,"activeIndex":3},"vars":[["hidden how","ABS · calipers · hydraulics"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":6,"narration":"Control returns: stopped. The complexity stayed hidden the whole time. That hidden \"how\" behind a simple \"what\" is abstraction.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":5,"activeIndex":4},"vars":[["↩ return","stopped"]]}]}]}}]]}]
